WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.083
Now let's run an INNER JOIN The patients table is
given the

00:00:05.109 --> 00:00:10.243
alias p and admissions is given the alias a The ON
condition

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.809
says an admission matches a patient when their
patient IDs are equal

00:00:15.643 --> 00:00:19.869
Run the query in the browser Then look at the
patient IDs

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:25.053
and admission IDs Notice that a patient with
multiple admissions appears more

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:29.895
than once That is expected because each result row
represents a matching

00:00:29.922 --> 00:00:35.815
admission Also look for the patient who has no
admission That

00:00:35.828 --> 00:00:39.183
patient should not appear because INNER JOIN
requires a match on both

00:00:39.209 --> 00:00:44.782
sides If you are practicing in pgAdmin use Copy and
paste the

00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:49.469
query into the Query Tool Before running it predict
roughly how many

00:00:49.495 --> 00:00:54.337
rows you expect After running it compare the number
of result rows

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:58.258
with the number of admissions in the database This
is a good

00:00:58.285 --> 00:01:00.284
first validation of the join grain
